Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-19-2000||12:21 AM||||OK I just cant stand it any more. After looking at Cooters and Oreifs super sweet rides, Ive decided its time to find an Indy style scoop. In case you havnt noticed, these things arent easy to find. Dosnt have to be an original Indy scoop, but one just like it would be great (for 85-88 V6 models).<BR>Any and all links and info for this would be greatly appriciated!!! TIA! Brian||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-19-2000||12:58 AM||||OK here it goes, IRM sells one for $200. The only other place I have seen them is from a place that calls them SD4 street scoops. Here is their link, I don't know what they charge. <P> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P>Finding a used one is going to be difficult since most people that have them want them.<BR>I also heard that FOCOA use to have some but I don't know if they still have them or not.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||phillip||06-19-2000||09:41 AM||||got mine from irm. i think focoa has them but for some reason they're about $100 more. don't know what the difference is.||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||06-19-2000||01:29 PM||||this may be a dumb question...       <P>will this scoop cause problems opening your hood?   and is this scoop functional?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Oreif||06-19-2000||02:34 PM||||Chris ~ It depends on how you mount it. Cooter has it mounted with the hinge and latch method. You open a latch and the scoop pops up and back to open the decklid. On my car 4 hex head bolt come off and I remove the entire scoop. It's a matter of preference.<BR>Both Cooter's and mine are functional. Making them functional is easy. just cut out the front part of the scoop and your decklid. See the thread:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004333.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004333.html</A> <P>for the different mounting and pics.<BR>||||reg||1
